# Styling

- Plain CSS in `src/styles`, one file per section. `src/index.css` only imports them, and the order of the imports is the cascade order.
- `responsive.css` and `accessibility.css` come last because they override the section files. Overrides for narrow screens, reduced motion, the contrast mode and the paused state go there.
- Colours, fonts and spacing come from the custom properties on `:root` in `base.css`. Add a property before repeating a literal colour.
- Themes and modes are classes on `<html>`: `light`, `contrast`, `still`, `xray`, plus `js`, `gl` or `nogl`, and `ready`. Style a mode by prefixing the selector with its class.
- The inline script in `index.html` sets `light` and `contrast` before first paint. A new persisted mode needs both that script and `remember` in `session.ts`.
- Fonts are Geist and Geist Mono. The WebGL headings measure text in Geist, so a font change must be checked against the canvas.
- Layouts must hold at 390 px wide with no horizontal page scroll. The single breakpoint is 820 px.
- Text and controls keep readable contrast in the dark, light and contrast modes.
